

From: juewang <juewang@linux.alibaba.com>

Use a single-use unpromoted input when MAX_EXPR and SAT_TRUNC are
supported for the narrower type, avoiding a redundant widen-and-narrow
sequence.

Changes since v1:
 v1: Add vect_sat_trunc_clip_input_vectype to check target support.
     Use the appropriate gimple_build_assign overload for MAX_EXPR.

gcc/ChangeLog:

	* tree-vect-patterns.cc (vect_sat_trunc_clip_input_vectype): New.
	(vect_recog_sat_trunc_pattern): Look through promotions and check
	target support for MAX_EXPR.

gcc/testsuite/ChangeLog:

	* gcc.target/riscv/rvv/autovec/pr120378-2.c: Dump optimized GIMPLE.
	* gcc.target/riscv/rvv/autovec/pr120378-3.c: Likewise.  Disable the
	vector cost model.
	* gcc.target/riscv/rvv/autovec/pr120378-4.c: Likewise.
	* gcc.target/riscv/rvv/autovec/sat-trunc-promote-1.c: New test.
	* gcc.target/riscv/rvv/autovec/sat-trunc-promote-run-1.c: New test.
